ere getting glued  on because the way that their ankles  would  they had to stand for the entire  application process with their ankles in  an unnatural position the days that we  don't have feet were really excited  number four Elijah Wood has an  incredible work ethic there was times  when we had time off Elijah pretty much  had no time off ever with that  incredible work ethic comes lack of  sleep but that didn't stop him I've seen  him fall down three sets of staircases  not even that could stop him and then  just get up and go  just woke up number five though Jon was  causing a lot of pain during his fight  scenes he was actually struggling too  it's pretty incredible how well his  fight scenes were considering he  couldn't really see anything John was  wearing a prosthetic that limited his  vision to this to make matters worse he  was allergic to the prosthetic skin he  was wearing and it made his eyes swell  up it was slightly sharp and he he had  no kind of you know sideway Vision it  also made his entire face super itchy  can you imagine at times you just wanted  to rip the damn stuff up and just  scratch  it made him develop topical eczema all  over his face I lost all skin in  it was like a skin peel then after a few  hours it would swell up and turn pink it  was itchy and painful and one felt very  very self-conscious number six  luck was definitely on his side that day  we had a stunt guy lined up to do this  sequence but Vigo wanted to do it  himself Vigo had to float down some  River Rapids in The Two Towers they had  safety guys do it beforehand to  calculate where he would float but it  wasn't exactly an accurate science well  they couldn't calculate and was the  weight of all the stuff there's just  things that changed the way it was for  me he didn't end up floating to the same  spot the guy before him did  spot where the current it's  a straight down  and before I knew it I was on the bottom  the current was so powerful it was  keeping him underwater nobody on set  could find him luckily he managed to  kick the wall and Propel himself out of  the current but it was a really scary  day on set number seven  apparently not your average Splinter  amazingly  Splinter I think probably made of  titanium when they were rehearsing for  the scene and Fellowship of the Ring  where they run to the Brandywine bridge  and jump onto the ferry Dominic Monahan  got a wooden Splinter deep into his foot  you think somebody cut his leg off if  the sweat was poor enough every time  he'd put pressure on his foot he was an  excruciating pain everyone thought this  was really something serious and they  did get this tiny Splinter Dominic ended  up keeping the Splinter he still has it  to this day  number eight Vigo gets a lot of injuries  on set his character naturally gets in a  lot of Sword fights with those sword  fights came a lot of Nicks to his hands  all his hands the the knuckles all had  chunks out of it because he was such a  committed actor he never flinched when  having to do another take no matter how  well you planned it you were always  getting Nicks and little abrasions that  were very painful number nine not really  ideal weather for a swim when Andy  Circus was supposed to shoot his scene  in The Two Towers where Gollum thrashes  around in the water the river was  actually frozen over so they brought a  crew of electricians to melt the snow  the snow was melted away but it didn't  necessarily make the water any warmer  when Andy first jumped into the water he  felt like he'd been punched in the chest  my heart felt like it just stopped  working I was instantly all the  extremities just froze up number 10.  nothing a bit of glue can't fix when  Vigo Mortensen was filming a sword fight  scene he got his tooth knocked into by  the end of the sword and his front tooth  just snapped in half and there's a big  chunk of tooth just broke off and fell  on the floor Migo didn't even care he  just picked it back up and said let's  keep it moving he said get some super  glue somebody get me some super glue I  can just stick it back on and carry on  shooting however they ended up rushing  him off for emergency dental work  instead  number 11 talk about bad luck in this  incident we have Sean Aston in  Fellowship of the Ring running through  the water in his prosthetic hobbit feet  unfortunately just a few steps in and  he's got a huge Shard of glass piercing  through the prosthetic and into his foot  the cut was so deep he had to miss the  rest of the day of filming to get 20  stitches number 12. a rough day at the  office for Orlando Bloom it was painful  it was very painful when filming The Two  Towers he was on his horse and ended up  getting thrown off with one of the  rib I was the first one to score an  injury and I think there was a little  bit of jealousy Orlando suffered through  it went and got it checked out and was  back on set the next morning now that's  stamina number 13. that really really  had to hurt can you try to kick the  helmet as close as possible to the lens  because it'll look great if it just like  flies past us Vigo Mortensen was given  four takes to get it right for this  scene in The Two Towers each take he  kind of got closer and closer to the  camera the fourth take I thought was  really good Peter Jackson thought one  more take and they'd have it he didn't  say anything to us but we found out that  Figo had actually broken two toes the  take was so good they ended up leaving  it in the movie  number 14. luckily no one was actually  injured but it could have been fatal  you're in the middle of fighting and  stuff and you look down and sure enough  there's the fins of a bomb sticking out  on the ground yep you heard that right  they were filming on some pretty  Dangerous Grounds this is a bomb this is  a rocket this is a all these things you  might find out here don't touch them to  make matters worse they were filming a  battle sequence so they were constantly  churning up the Earth with every move  the Army would come intermittently to  clear away the explosives but there were  always some still buried in the ground  number 15 the amount of stunt work in  rings of power is actually pretty insane  lead stunt performer Dana Grant was  admitted to hospital after a head injury  on set she's an award-winning veteran  stunt performer who feels most calm when  she's lit on fire I feel quite at ease  when I do it after treatment at the  hospital it was revealed that she ended  up suffering a concussion as well as  having to get surgery months after the  show wrapped Alyssa Cadwell a  professional stunt performer actor and  Dancer she even doubled for Nicole  Kidman and Aquaman was also badly  injured on the set of rings of power the  scene involved her falling into a large  water tank but unfortunately her head  struck a bolt in the process she was  unable to come back to work for months  luckily she's okay but it was definitely  a traumatic experience  broken toes chipped teeth painful  allergies avoiding landmines and several  hospital visits later we've got the  entire Lord of the Rings franchise and  TV show to binge what do you think was  the most painful scene to film

